1
00:00:07,610 --> 00:00:12,550
A quiz question: 3 quarters times 17, plus 3 quarters times 3.

2
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:15,840
You have 10 seconds, and no paper.

3
00:00:15,890 --> 00:00:17,120
What is the answer?

4
00:00:17,170 --> 00:00:20,680
Pause the video and work it out.

5
00:00:20,730 --> 00:00:22,900
Both parts have 3 quarters.

6
00:00:22,950 --> 00:00:27,280
So take it out: 3 quarters times, bracket, 17 plus 3.

7
00:00:27,330 --> 00:00:30,970
That is 3 quarters of 20, which is 15.

8
00:00:31,020 --> 00:00:36,750
Remember: A times B, plus A times C, equals A times, bracket, B plus C.

9
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:43,080
For example, 7 times 23, plus 7 times 77, is 7 times 100, which is 700.

10
00:00:43,130 --> 00:00:46,960
Here are some ways to make fraction calculations easier.

11
00:00:47,010 --> 00:00:50,900
Take out a common factor, like the quiz question.

12
00:00:50,950 --> 00:00:57,260
Cancel before multiplying, as in 14 fifteenths times 25 twenty-eighths.

13
00:00:57,310 --> 00:00:58,960
14 and 28 share 14.

14
00:00:59,010 --> 00:01:00,570
25 and 15 share 5.

15
00:01:00,620 --> 00:01:05,950
That leaves 1 third times 5 halves, which is 5 sixths.

16
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:08,320
And use whole minus a part.

17
00:01:08,370 --> 00:01:13,040
7 eighths of 48 is the whole 48, minus 1 eighth of 48.

18
00:01:13,090 --> 00:01:16,390
That is 48 minus 6, which is 42.

19
00:01:16,440 --> 00:01:17,210
Your turn.

20
00:01:17,260 --> 00:01:18,920
Find 9 tenths of 250.

21
00:01:18,970 --> 00:01:22,520
Pause the video and try it.

22
00:01:22,570 --> 00:01:24,860
1 tenth of 250 is 25.

23
00:01:24,910 --> 00:01:30,100
So 9 tenths is 250 minus 25, which is 225.

24
00:01:30,150 --> 00:01:32,990
The order of operations still applies.

25
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:34,820
Multiply before you add.

26
00:01:34,870 --> 00:01:41,680
1 half plus 1 third times 3 quarters is 1 half plus 1 quarter, which is 3 quarters.

27
00:01:41,730 --> 00:01:43,520
But brackets come first.

28
00:01:43,570 --> 00:01:49,900
1 half plus 1 third, in a bracket, times 6, is 5 sixths times 6, which is 5.

29
00:01:49,950 --> 00:01:51,220
Here is the method.

30
00:01:51,270 --> 00:01:54,890
Step 1: look for a common factor to take out.

31
00:01:54,940 --> 00:01:58,070
Step 2: cancel before you multiply.

32
00:01:58,120 --> 00:02:02,490
Step 3: re-order the numbers, or use whole minus a part.

33
00:02:02,540 --> 00:02:07,760
Step 4: follow the order of operations, and check with an estimate.

34
00:02:07,810 --> 00:02:12,480
Work out 18 thirty-fifths times 21 twenty-fourths.

35
00:02:12,530 --> 00:02:15,790
18 and 24 share 6, leaving 3 and 4.

36
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:19,640
21 and 35 share 7, leaving 3 and 5.

37
00:02:19,690 --> 00:02:23,650
3 fifths times 3 quarters is 9 twentieths.

38
00:02:23,700 --> 00:02:24,460
Your turn.

39
00:02:24,510 --> 00:02:28,150
Work out 10 twenty-firsts times 14 fifteenths.

40
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:31,320
Pause and work it out.

41
00:02:31,370 --> 00:02:34,540
10 and 15 share 5, leaving 2 and 3.

42
00:02:34,590 --> 00:02:37,760
14 and 21 share 7, leaving 2 and 3.

43
00:02:37,810 --> 00:02:43,090
So it is 2 thirds times 2 thirds, which is 4 ninths.

44
00:02:43,140 --> 00:02:48,160
Work out 4 times 2 and 3 eighths, plus 4 times 1 and 5 eighths.

45
00:02:48,210 --> 00:02:54,430
Take out the 4: 4 times, bracket, 2 and 3 eighths plus 1 and 5 eighths.

46
00:02:54,480 --> 00:02:56,620
The bracket is exactly 4.

47
00:02:56,670 --> 00:02:58,920
And 4 times 4 is 16.

48
00:02:58,970 --> 00:03:02,530
Max works out 1 third plus 2 thirds times 1 half.

49
00:03:02,580 --> 00:03:05,140
Which line goes wrong first?

50
00:03:05,190 --> 00:03:06,380
Line 1 is wrong.

51
00:03:06,430 --> 00:03:09,270
Multiplication comes before addition.

52
00:03:09,320 --> 00:03:12,390
2 thirds times 1 half is 1 third.

53
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:16,020
Then 1 third plus 1 third is 2 thirds.

54
00:03:16,070 --> 00:03:19,360
A shop has a sale: everything is 1 quarter off.

55
00:03:19,410 --> 00:03:22,390
So you pay 3 quarters of the price.

56
00:03:22,440 --> 00:03:26,900
You buy a 36 dollar shirt and a 44 dollar pair of jeans.

57
00:03:26,950 --> 00:03:33,160
Instead of two calculations, add first: 3 quarters of 80 is 60 dollars.

58
00:03:33,210 --> 00:03:34,520
One last question.

59
00:03:34,570 --> 00:03:37,470
What is 1 half minus 1 quarter times 2?

60
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:40,910
Pause the video and answer.

61
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:42,110
Multiply first.

62
00:03:42,160 --> 00:03:44,360
1 quarter times 2 is 1 half.

63
00:03:44,410 --> 00:03:47,320
Then 1 half minus 1 half is 0.

64
00:03:47,370 --> 00:03:52,360
To remember: take out common factors, using the distributive law.

65
00:03:52,410 --> 00:03:54,860
Cancel before multiplying.

66
00:03:54,910 --> 00:03:58,110
Use whole minus a part, and re-ordering.

67
00:03:58,160 --> 00:04:01,280
The order of operations still applies.

68
00:04:01,330 --> 00:04:06,510
Great work! Now practise lesson 7.6 on Camday.
